WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:03.287
It's late. Your eBay listing shows one left.

2
00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:07.091
At your supplier's Shopify store, that same variant just sold out.

3
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.505
eBay still shows one. And you're asleep, at work, or driving.

4
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.820
A buyer taps Buy It Now.

5
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:19.239
Your supplier has none left. You cancel, and that can count against your seller performance.

6
00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:21.820
This is ELM Easy Monitoring.

7
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:28.220
Your suppliers change stock. ELM keeps watching, and your eBay quantities stay in step when the checks pass.

8
00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:32.755
At launch, you connect eBay yourself, on eBay's own sign in page.

9
00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:40.128
ELM reads your listings and every variation. That works today, shown in the real engine with sample data.

10
00:00:41.433 --> 00:00:47.189
At launch, you add suppliers by pasting product links, or browse their catalogs inside ELM.

11
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.142
Today, ELM already monitors every variant on its own: each color, each size.

12
00:00:54.533 --> 00:01:00.678
Each eBay variation links to its exact supplier variant. Navy / M is not Navy / L.

13
00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:09.838
When SKUs match exactly, ELM suggests the link and you verify it. Sync then starts by itself, after the next successful check.

14
00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:16.452
At launch, ELM also matches by options and title, with bulk accept and a review queue.

15
00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:20.087
Now the sync. A supplier variant sells out.

16
00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:26.382
On the next check, ELM sets eBay from one to zero, with Out-of-Stock Control keeping the listing live.

17
00:01:26.967 --> 00:01:31.352
When it's back, a second check, at least ten minutes later, puts it back to one.

18
00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:37.930
Every decision has a recorded reason. And dry run shows changes before anything is sent.

19
00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:43.520
So you can step away. Checks run on a schedule, every hour by default.

20
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:49.262
If a check fails, ELM holds the last quantity for up to 24 hours, instead of guessing.

21
00:01:49.867 --> 00:01:56.539
Telegram alerts reach you when something needs you: a failed eBay update, your own edit, or a listing to review.

22
00:01:57.333 --> 00:02:01.360
It all lives in one dashboard, with an audit trail of every change.

23
00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:12.248
At launch: automatic SKUs, bulk import and bulk management, more than one eBay account, and plans you manage yourself.

24
00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:19.354
And auto listing. Start from a supplier's website, browse the catalog, and set a supplier price range.

25
00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:27.079
Select products, and ELM prepares drafts, with images matched to each variation and a SKU for every one.

26
00:02:27.867 --> 00:02:33.806
You review every draft and publish only what you approve. Eligible listings then join stock sync.

27
00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:41.253
ELM only changes quantity. It never buys from your suppliers, and never ends or reprices your listings.

28
00:02:41.333 --> 00:02:45.157
Spend less time checking suppliers, and more time growing your store.

29
00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:49.275
Join the early access waitlist. The link is on screen.
